{
  "_sheet": "materials",
  "_doc": "One row per surface material the course and terrain use. albedo/normal/weather are content.json ids; uv_scale is metres per texture tile. Course.gd draws every textured row with one weathering shader: weather is a second texture mixed in by noise over weather_cover of the surface, grime is the strength of dirt streaks running down from a ramp's top edge (and its chipped lip), detail is the close-up detail overlay that keeps the texture sharp under the player. filter: aniso = mipmapped anisotropic (every shader material samples this way since world_r1).",
